    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(4) Section 5",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-5-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a03367.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a03367.pdf, p.5",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where, before the commencement time, the former Commission had\ncommenced to perform, in relation to a particular matter, a function\nconferred on the former Commission by the repealed Act, but had not\ncompleted the performance of that function—\n\nHuman Rights and Equal Opportunity Commission\n(Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments)\nNo. 126, 1986\n(a) the Commission may continue and complete the performance of\nthat function in relation to that matter as if the Commission Act\nhad been in force at the time when the former\nCommission\ncommenced to perform the function; and\n(b) for the purposes of the performance of that function under paragraph\n(a), references in the Commission Act to a matter under examination\nor inquiry shall be read as including references to a matter under\nexamination or inquiry by the Commission\npursuant to\nthat\nparagraph.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where, before the commencement time, the former Commission had\ncommenced to perform, in relation to a particular matter, a function\nconferred on the former Commission by the repealed Act, but had not\ncompleted the performance of that function—\n\nHuman Rights and Equal Opportunity Commission\n(Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments)\nNo. 126, 1986\n(a) the Commission may continue and complete the performance of\nthat function in relation to that matter as if the Commission Act\nhad been in force at the time when the former\nCommission\ncommenced to perform the function; and\n(b) for the purposes of the performance of that function under paragraph\n(a), references in the Commission Act to a matter under examination\nor inquiry shall be read as including references to a matter under\nexamination or inquiry by the Commission\npursuant to\nthat\nparagraph.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ebd03e0791b738817f77e95cfc1bfba671730da0892bb21fc4dd5a8faed35b5d",
      "skos:note": "Commission may not complete performance of function before commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-5-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(4) Section 5",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 5,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where, before the commencement time, the former Commission had\ncommenced to perform, in relation to a particular matter, a function\nconferred on the former Commission by the repealed Act, but had not\ncompleted the performance of that function—\n\nHuman Rights and Equal Opportunity Commission\n(Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments)\nNo. 126, 1986\n(a) the Commission may continue and complete the performance of\nthat function in relation to that matter as if the Commission Act\nhad been in force at the time when the former\nCommission\ncommenced to perform the function; and\n(b) for the purposes of the performance of that function under paragraph\n(a), references in the Commission Act to a matter under examination\nor inquiry shall be read as including references to a matter under\nexamination or inquiry by the Commission\npursuant to\nthat\nparagraph."
    },
    {
