    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(5) Section 5",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-5-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a03367.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a03367.pdf, p.5",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where, before the commencement time, a person had commenced\nto inquire into an act or practice, or to investigate a particular aspect of an\nact or practice, pursuant to a resolution by the former Commission under\nsub-section 13 (1) of the repealed Act but had not completed the inquiry or\ninvestigation, the person may, after the commencement time, continue and\ncomplete the inquiry or investigation as if the power to inquire into that act\nor practice, or investigate that act or practice, had been delegated to the\nperson under section 19 of the Commission Act.\nInter-governmental arrangements",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Where, before the commencement time, a person had commenced\nto inquire into an act or practice, or to investigate a particular aspect of an\nact or practice, pursuant to a resolution by the former Commission under\nsub-section 13 (1) of the repealed Act but had not completed the inquiry or\ninvestigation, the person may, after the commencement time, continue and\ncomplete the inquiry or investigation as if the power to inquire into that act\nor practice, or investigate that act or practice, had been delegated to the\nperson under section 19 of the Commission Act.\nInter-governmental arrangements",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "389f392a265ab1aa4fcc2d31ba9ca2265a1e542db8bc91432841e974d53e6275",
      "skos:note": "Continue and complete inquiry or investigation after commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-5-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(5) Section 5",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 5,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where, before the commencement time, a person had commenced\nto inquire into an act or practice, or to investigate a particular aspect of an\nact or practice, pursuant to a resolution by the former Commission under\nsub-section 13 (1) of the repealed Act but had not completed the inquiry or\ninvestigation, the person may, after the commencement time, continue and\ncomplete the inquiry or investigation as if the power to inquire into that act\nor practice, or investigate that act or practice, had been delegated to the\nperson under section 19 of the Commission Act.\nInter-governmental arrangements"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-5-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
