      "cml:conclusionText": "A publication of a notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(2) Section 47",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-47-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a03367.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a03367.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A notice in relation to a complaint, being a notice served on the\nCommissioner under sub-section 52 (4) of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984\nbefore the commencement time, shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to require the Commissioner to refer the complaint to the\nCommission.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A notice in relation to a complaint, being a notice served on the\nCommissioner under sub-section 52 (4) of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984\nbefore the commencement time, shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to require the Commissioner to refer the complaint to the\nCommission.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b3229461351b11d681448bafdb65a7c26db93185d72e5e85986f1bc485a283bc",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner must refer complaint to Commission after notice served before commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-47-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(2) Section 47",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A notice in relation to a complaint, being a notice served on the\nCommissioner under sub-section 52 (4) of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984\nbefore the commencement time, shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to require the Commissioner to refer the complaint to the\nCommission."
    },
    {
