      "cml:premiseText": "Notice served before commencement time",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Commissioner must refer complaint"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(3) Section 47",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-47-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a03367.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a03367.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where—\n(a) within\nthe\nperiod\nof\ndays\nimmediately\npreceding\nthe\ncommencement time, the former Commission served notice on a\nperson under section 87 of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984; and\n(b) at the commencement time, the person had not complied with the\nrequirement made by the notice,\nthe requirement made by the notice shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to be a requirement to disclose to the Commission, before the\nexpiration of the period of 28 days after the notice was served, the\ninformation specified in the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Where—\n(a) within\nthe\nperiod\nof\ndays\nimmediately\npreceding\nthe\ncommencement time, the former Commission served notice on a\nperson under section 87 of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984; and\n(b) at the commencement time, the person had not complied with the\nrequirement made by the notice,\nthe requirement made by the notice shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to be a requirement to disclose to the Commission, before the\nexpiration of the period of 28 days after the notice was served, the\ninformation specified in the notice.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee8bd969498156134706e5002ea7de5a98aa5823117ff0cb67d09915dddf8fae",
      "skos:note": "Requirement to disclose information after notice served",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a03367#sec-47-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(3) Section 47",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where—\n(a) within\nthe\nperiod\nof\ndays\nimmediately\npreceding\nthe\ncommencement time, the former Commission served notice on a\nperson under section 87 of the Sex Discrimination\nAct 1984; and\n(b) at the commencement time, the person had not complied with the\nrequirement made by the notice,\nthe requirement made by the notice shall, after the commencement time, be\ndeemed to be a requirement to disclose to the Commission, before the\nexpiration of the period of 28 days after the notice was served, the\ninformation specified in the notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a03367-sec-47-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
